{# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   SITE-WIDE SEARCH

   One box that reaches nominees, results, posts, events, threads, profiles,
   phase changes, award programmes, categories and the site's own pages. It is
   the /activity engine — the same ActivityFeedService, the same AI intent pass
   — surfaced from the header instead of only from one page.

   ── THE ACCESSIBILITY IS THE FEATURE, NOT A COATING ──────────────────────────

   • It is a real <dialog>-shaped modal: focus MOVES into the input on open,
     is TRAPPED while open, and RETURNS to the button that opened it on close.
     A search overlay that leaves focus behind it is unusable by keyboard —
     you tab into a list you cannot see.
   • The input is a WAI-ARIA 1.2 combobox: aria-expanded, aria-controls,
     aria-autocomplete=list, aria-activedescendant, role=listbox/option.
   • The active option moves with aria-activedescendant, never with focus().
     Moving real focus into the list takes it out of the input, so the next
     keystroke goes somewhere the user is not looking and typing "vote" after
     arrowing down loses the "e".
   • Results arriving is announced on a polite live region that is ALWAYS in
     the DOM. A live region inserted at the same moment as its text is not
     reliably announced — the observer has nothing to observe yet.
   • Escape closes. Enter opens the active result, or submits to /activity when
     nothing is active, so the box always has a destination.

   ── AND THE AI IS BOUNDED ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

   The model reads the QUERY for intent ("winners in Ghana last month" → a kind,
   a country, a date range). It never writes a result. Everything on screen came
   out of the database; if the model is off, over budget or wrong, the search
   degrades to plain text matching and still answers. That is why interpretation
   is a filter and not a generator.
   ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ #}
<div class="ags" id="agSearch" hidden data-ag-search>
  <div class="ags__scrim" data-ag-search-close></div>

  <div class="ags__panel" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="agsTitle">
    <h2 class="sr-only" id="agsTitle">Search Africa GATES</h2>

    {# A real GET form: with no JavaScript this still submits to /activity, which
       renders the same results server-side. The overlay is an enhancement. #}
    <form class="ags__bar" method="get" action="/activity" role="search">
      <svg class="ags__icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="7"/><path d="m20 20-3.6-3.6" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
      <label class="sr-only" for="agsInput">Search nominees, events, posts and pages</label>
      <input class="ags__input" id="agsInput" name="q" type="search" autocomplete="off"
             spellcheck="false" placeholder="Search nominees, events, pages…"
             aria-describedby="agsHint">
      <button type="button" class="ags__close" data-ag-search-close aria-label="Close search">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="m6 6 12 12M18 6 6 18" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
      </button>
    </form>

    <p class="ags__hint" id="agsHint">Try a name, a category, or a question like “how does voting work”.</p>

    {# Always present, so the announcement lands. Empty until there is something
       true to say — a status line that says "0 results" before you have typed is
       noise read out on every open. #}
    <p class="ags__status" id="agsStatus" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></p>

    {# No role="listbox" in the markup. ag-search.js adds it, along with the
       combobox roles on the input, because the two only make sense together: an
       input that advertises a popup it cannot open, or a list that claims to hold
       options when nothing will ever put any in it, is a promise to a screen
       reader that the page cannot keep if the script fails to load. The honest
       degraded state is a plain search field that submits to /activity.
       ActivityPageAccessibilityTest enforces this rule for the whole page. #}
    <ul class="ags__list" id="agsResults"></ul>

    <p class="ags__foot">
      <kbd>↑</kbd><kbd>↓</kbd> to move · <kbd>Enter</kbd> to open · <kbd>Esc</kbd> to close
      <a href="/activity">Full search →</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
